                    response: I propose fine-tuning a                           
                    pretrained EfficientNet-B0 from the                         
                    timm library to classify malignant                          
                    versus non-malignant lesions by                             
                    replacing its head with a single                            
                    output for malignancy probability.                          
                    We’ll use standard augmentations                            
                    including random resized crop and                           
                    horizontal flips, normalize images,                         
                    and perform an 80/20 stratified split                       
