                    Design: I propose to improve robustness                     
                    and generalization by ensembling five                       
                    models trained on different stratified                      
                    folds. We’ll perform 5-fold                                 
                    cross-validation, training a Swin                           
                    Transformer model on each fold, saving                      
                    each checkpoint, and computing                              
                    out‐of‐fold ROC AUC across the full                         
                    dataset. At inference, our `predict`                        
                    function will load all five models and                      
                    average their malignancy probabilities.                     
                    This ensemble approach typically yields                     
                    a substantial boost in test‐time AUROC                      
                    with only modest code changes.                              
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without errors. The model                      
                    was trained using 5-fold                                    
                    cross-validation with a Swin                                
                    Transformer Tiny architecture and mixup                     
                    augmentation. The validation ROC AUC                        
                    scores for each fold ranged from                            
                    approximately 0.9263 to 0.9463, with an                     
                    overall out-of-fold ROC AUC of 0.9367,                      
                    indicating strong performance in                            
                    classifying malignant vs benign                             
                    lesions. The model weights were saved                       
                    correctly, and a prediction function is                     
                    provided for inference on new images.                       
                    Validation Metric: 0.9367                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose adding RandomErasing                      
                    augmentation to the training pipeline                       
                    to improve robustness to occlusions and                     
                    color variations. This atomic change                        
                    only modifies the train_transform,                          
                    inserting a RandomErasing step after                        
                    normalization. The rest of the 5‐fold                       
                    CV ensembling pipeline remains                              
                    unchanged to isolate the effect of this                     
                    augmentation. We retrain the models and                     
                    report updated fold and overall ROC                         
                    AUC.                                                        
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors or                          
                    bugs. The model was trained using a                         
                    5-fold cross-validation approach with a                     
                    Swin Transformer Tiny model, achieving                      
                    strong performance with individual fold                     
                    ROC AUC scores ranging from about                           
                    0.9334 to 0.9432. The overall                               
                    out-of-fold ROC AUC score was 0.9355,                       
                    indicating a high-quality classifier                        
                    for the malignant vs. benign skin                           
                    lesion classification task. The script                      
                    also saved the trained models for                           
                    ensemble prediction.                                        
                    Validation Metric: 0.9355                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose incorporating simple                      
                    horizontal‐flip test‐time augmentation                      
                    (TTA) during both validation and                            
                    inference. For each batch of validation                     
                    images, we will compute model outputs                       
                    on the original and horizontally                            
                    flipped versions, average the logits,                       
                    then apply the sigmoid to get                               
                    probabilities. The same TTA logic is                        
                    added to the `predict()` function so                        
                    that ensemble predictions leverage both                     
                    views for improved robustness. This                         
                    atomic change requires minimal code                         
                    adjustments yet often yields a                              
                    consistent boost in ROC AUC.                                
                    Results: The training script                                
                    successfully trained a Swin Transformer                     
                    Tiny model with 5-fold cross-validation                     
                    on the skin lesion dataset. The model                       
                    used mixup augmentation, class-balanced                     
                    sampling, and horizontal-flip test-time                     
                    augmentation. The validation ROC AUC                        
                    scores across folds were consistently                       
                    high (around 0.94), and the overall                         
                    out-of-fold ROC AUC was 0.9412,                             
                    indicating strong predictive                                
                    performance for malignancy                                  
                    classification. The model checkpoints                       
                    were saved correctly for ensemble                           
                    prediction.                                                 
                    Validation Metric: 0.9412                                   
                                                                                
